<section class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
        <h1 class="page-head__title">About Vylen Linux</h1>
        <p class="page-head__lead">
            An independent, source-based Linux distribution with its own package manager.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <div class="container about-intro">
        <p class="about-intro__lead">
            Vylen Linux is an independent, source-based distribution. It ships its own package manager,
            <strong>Emerald</strong>, and public ports repositories. Ports are built from source on the user's machine;
            the bootstrap rootfs is distributed separately as a prebuilt base.
        </p>

        <p class="about-intro__text">
            It is built for experienced users who want to construct their system by hand and keep control over its
            configuration. Vylen uses <strong>systemd</strong> as its init system, and Emerald manages the port build workflow.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head">
            <span class="section-head__eyebrow">At a glance</span>
            <h2 class="section-title">Key characteristics</h2>
            <p class="section-head__subtitle">The core traits that define how Vylen works.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="features">
            {% for item in highlights %}
                <article class="feature-card">
                    <div class="feature-card__icon">{{ item.icon | icon(20) }}</div>
                    <h3 class="feature-card__title">{{ item.title }}</h3>

                    <p class="feature-card__description">{{ item.description }}</p>
                </article>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head">
            <span class="section-head__eyebrow">Principles</span>
            <h2 class="section-title">What Vylen stands for</h2>
            <p class="section-head__subtitle">The design choices that guide every decision in the distribution.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="principles">
            {% for principle in principles %}
                <article class="principle">
                    <span class="principle__number">{{ loop.index | padNumber }}</span>
                    <h3 class="principle__title">{{ principle.title }}</h3>
                    <p class="principle__text">{{ principle.text }}</p>
                </article>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <div class="container emerald">
        <div class="emerald__content">
            <span class="section-head__eyebrow">Emerald</span>
            <h2 class="section-title">A source-based package manager</h2>

            <p class="section-text">
                Emerald handles dependency resolution, source fetching, checksums, compilation, and installation. Creating
                custom ports and repositories is straightforward. The build template resembles PKGBUILD from Arch Linux and
                CRUX, but is written entirely in POSIX shell.
            </p>

            <ul class="check-list">
                <li>Dependency-aware builds from source</li>
                <li>POSIX shell build templates (CRUX-like)</li>
                <li>Custom build flags per package</li>
                <li>System-wide upgrades in one command</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="terminal">
            <div class="terminal__bar">
                <span class="terminal__dot terminal__dot--red"></span>
                <span class="terminal__dot terminal__dot--yellow"></span>
                <span class="terminal__dot terminal__dot--green"></span>

                <span class="terminal__title">~ : fish</span>
            </div>

            <pre class="terminal__body">
<span class="terminal__prompt">root@vylen $</span> emerald install vivaldi -q</span>
==> Building: vivaldi-8.1.4087.56-1
==> Source found: /var/cache/emerald/sources/vivaldi-8.1.4087.56.rpm
==> Checking checksums...
==> Unpacking: /var/cache/emerald/sources/vivaldi-8.1.4087.56.rpm
==> Preparing: /usr/ports/extra/vivaldi/0001-add-support-for-user-flags.patch
==> Build start: vivaldi-8.1.4087.56-1
==> Build success: vivaldi-8.1.4087.56-1
==> Packaging success: vivaldi-8.1.4087.56-1.epkg.tar.xz (132M)
install: vivaldi-8.1.4087.56-1...
<span class="terminal__ok">==></span> Updating desktop file MIME type cache...</span>
<span class="terminal__ok">==></span> Updating icon theme caches...</span>
<span class="terminal__prompt">root@vylen $</span></pre>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <div class="container cta">
        <div class="cta__content">
            <h2 class="cta__title">Ready to take control?</h2>
            <p class="cta__subtitle">Grab the rootfs tarball and build a system that's truly yours.</p>
        </div>

        <a href="#/download" class="btn btn--primary btn--lg">Download Vylen</a>
    </div>
</section>
